-- title:
--   Witt coefficients mod p from a ghost component mod p^N
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime number. Assume that the image of $p$ in $S$ is a non-zero-divisor, and that the quotient ring $S/(p)$, where $(p)$ is the ideal generated by the image of $p$, is reduced. Let $z$ be a Witt vector in $W(S) =$ `WittVector p S`, and let $N$ be a natural number. Suppose that the ghost component of $z$ of index $N-1$ (natural subtraction, so index $0$ when $N = 0$), that is $\sum_{j<N} p^{j} z_j^{p^{N-1-j}}$ for $N \ge 1$, lies in the ideal generated by $p^N$ in $S$. Then for every natural number $j$ with $j < N$, the $j$-th Witt coefficient `z.coeff j` lies in the ideal generated by $p$ in $S$. For $N = 0$ the conclusion is vacuous, so no content is asserted about the hypothesis in that degenerate case.
--
--   This is the injectivity statement underlying Fontaine's comparison between ghost components and Witt covectors: over a ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor and whose reduction mod $p$ is reduced, the $(N-1)$-st ghost component taken modulo $p^N$ controls the first $N$ Witt coefficients modulo $p$. It is used in the treatment of logarithm covectors of formal groups and of deformations, being cited by [`MvFormalGroup.coeff_map_subst_sub_map_sub_map_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.coeff_map_subst_sub_map_sub_map_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector), [`MvFormalGroup.coeff_sub_coeff_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_le`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.coeff_sub_coeff_mem_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector_of_le) and [`Deformation.map_coeff_mem_span_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector`](thm.html#Deformation.map_coeff_mem_span_of_forall_coeff_ghostComponent_eq_logCovector).
-- source:
